From c874a3c6d2789f24cb6def3f19806328494084c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Certified LM head: MTP draft top-1 and DFlash greedy draft
 projection

Behind SGLANG_CERTIFIED_HEAD_DRAFT (off by default):

- MTP draft steps inside the EAGLE draft CUDA graph: the draft model's
  logits processor captures the certified head under a device flag and the
  stock head under its negation, and draft_topk1 replaces
  draft_topk1_postprocess with two conditional nodes, the stock top-1 under
  the negated flag and, under the flag, the certified ids with the same side
  effects (positions advanced, draft token column written).
- MTP draft extend (the first draft token of a round): the certified ids
  are attached to the replay's output and replace the argmax outside the
  graph.
- DFlash's _DflashDraftSampler (tp=1, no vocabulary offset): the in-graph
  projection writes its output from the certified head or from the stock
  matmul and argmax.

Top-1 drafting is greedy whatever the requests' sampling parameters, so the
MTP gates are set for every batch unless rejection sampling samples draft
proposals. Each call checks that the draft reads the target's head tensor,
so the fallback reads the bytes the stock drafter reads. Check mode covers
the draft paths as well.
